1
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:44,020
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:46,880
[Episode 22]

3
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,800
Why does this smell so foul?

4
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:11,590
Is it ready now or not?

5
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,080
Look who you're asking.

6
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,540
How would I possibly know?

7
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,960
Just boil it a little longer.

8
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,420
Won't it get even thicker?

9
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,310
It'll look even more awful.

10
00:02:21,310 --> 00:02:22,520
I heard from Ai Chen

11
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:25,079
that she put a lot of effort

12
00:02:26,590 --> 00:02:28,470
into curing you.

13
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,680
Do you know that?

14
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:32,910
I know.

15
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,120
Are you moved?

16
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:36,710
A little.

17
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,400
Just a little?

18
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:41,110
Just a little.

19
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,040
A little also counts.

20
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:47,560
But I heard that

21
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:51,120
you haven't been very cooperative.

22
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:53,190
That's not true.

23
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,060
It's just too hard to cure my illness.

24
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:59,079
No matter what, you must accept treatment.

25
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:02,190
Sit closer.

26
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:11,630
A bit closer.

27
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,560
I also heard that

28
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,680
you've made up your mind.

29
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,240
Mm-hmm.

30
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,630
I want to treat this illness,

31
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:29,150
but it can't be cured.

32
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:31,120
That's not a contradiction, right?

33
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,650
And I also heard from Ai Chen

34
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,870
that Mrs. Mi Si also has kleptomania.

35
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:35,430
Why haven't you

36
00:03:35,430 --> 00:03:36,750
gotten it treated all these years?

37
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:38,750
Liu Zhengliang! Come take a look!

38
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,150
S-She's calling me over.

39
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:41,480
I'm going to take a look.

40
00:03:43,750 --> 00:03:46,280
It's going to burn on the bottom
if we keep boiling it, right?

41
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:47,079
What's wrong?

42
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:48,840
See if it's done.

43
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,470
I can't tell

44
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:51,520
if it's done either.

45
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,360
Fine.

46
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,800
I'll just leave it at this state.

47
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,590
We might as well give it a shot.

48
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,520
Here you are. Bottoms up.

49
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:01,360
Wait, what do you mean?

50
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,630
There's some for me, too?

51
00:04:02,630 --> 00:04:03,680
Yes, of course.

52
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:05,150
One bowl for you, and one for me.

53
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:06,470
It cures any disease.

54
00:04:06,590 --> 00:04:07,400
No, no...

55
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:09,030
Didn't you get

56
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:10,080
this folk remedy to cure

57
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,870
your nausea
whenever you see written words?

58
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:13,000
Mine is for that.

59
00:04:13,150 --> 00:04:15,150
Yours is for treating your fear of snow.

60
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:16,160
We both have to drink it.

61
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,490
But they're different.

62
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,390
I-I can't drink this kind

63
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:21,040
of stuff with unknown ingredients.

64
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:21,839
Just drink it.

65
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,240
It won't kill you.

66
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:25,370
That still doesn't mean I can drink it.

67
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,830
Besides, it might kill me.

68
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,680
I advise you not to drink it either.

69
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:31,760
Liu Zhengliang.

70
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,480
I really appreciate how you treat patients

71
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,800
ridiculously.

72
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,390
However,

73
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:40,830
you need to care more

74
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:42,159
about your own illness.

75
00:04:42,430 --> 00:04:43,270
You need to be

76
00:04:43,270 --> 00:04:44,750
as brave as I am.

77
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:45,720
Cheers.

78
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,240
Did you mean "meticulously"?

79
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:55,600
T-This is not

80
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,730
a matter of bravery.

81
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,160
I won't force you to drink it.

82
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:04,830
Don't...

83
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:08,070
Look.

84
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,820
She set an example for you.

85
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:10,630
Drink it.

86
00:05:37,190 --> 00:05:38,000
Sorry.

87
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:40,740
[1314 Funeral Supplies]
[Xiaoximen Store]

88
00:05:51,390 --> 00:05:52,250
How do you feel?

89
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,270
A bit better.

90
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:57,250
What did I tell you?

91
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,730
You can't drink random things, right?

92
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:01,600
You did say that.

93
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:02,400
This thing...

94
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:06,080
It's good as long as it works.

95
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:07,560
I used to

96
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:10,270
throw up after reading too much.

97
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:12,480
Now, I already feel nauseous

98
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,880
before I even open a book.

99
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,270
Still so obstinate.

100
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:17,830
Wipe it.

101
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,800
Listen.

102
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,540
Do you think I was messing around?

103
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,120
Mine was medicine.

104
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:26,830
What I gave you was

105
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:28,270
a winter melon
and tangerine peel Americano,

106
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:29,040
okay?

107
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:29,950
Just to give you

108
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:31,630
a little placebo effect.

109
00:06:35,950 --> 00:06:36,630
Well,

110
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:37,480
placebo effect

111
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,720
only works

112
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,720
if I believe it.

113
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,800
You.

114
00:06:45,159 --> 00:06:46,240
Come out with me.

115
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,360
What are you doing?

116
00:06:48,190 --> 00:06:49,050
What am I doing?

117
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:49,600
Just for a chat.

118
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,659
Alright, alright.

119
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:53,120
D-Don't give him a hard time.

120
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,310
Stay out of this.

121
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,830
This is a conversation

122
00:06:58,360 --> 00:06:59,190
between men.

123
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,360
Let's go.

124
00:07:09,950 --> 00:07:11,550
Will they fight to the death?

125
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,850
Your dad knows what he's doing.

126
00:07:14,430 --> 00:07:15,820
I'm feeling so nauseous.

127
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:19,570
[Burial Items]

128
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,310
Don't be nervous.

129
00:07:25,750 --> 00:07:26,800
I'm not nervous.

130
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,070
Well,

131
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,680
if you want to beat me up,

132
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:32,070
just do it.

133
00:07:32,390 --> 00:07:33,830
I can't beat you anyway,

134
00:07:33,950 --> 00:07:35,150
so I won't fight back.

135
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,680
Why would I beat you up?

136
00:07:38,310 --> 00:07:39,680
I know I'm annoying.

137
00:07:40,070 --> 00:07:42,270
No one has ever liked me
since I was a kid.

138
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,140
I don't know about others,

139
00:07:46,870 --> 00:07:50,240
but I'm really fond of you.

140
00:07:58,159 --> 00:07:59,360
What you're saying is...

141
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:01,160
is giving me goosebumps.

142
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,240
I have my principles.

143
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:05,830
I like whoever

144
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:07,070
my daughter likes.

145
00:08:08,510 --> 00:08:09,390
Besides,

146
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:12,830
you're

147
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:14,520
quite an honest guy.

148
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:15,830
This is good.

149
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:23,200
Then... Then why did you ask me out?

150
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:38,510
I've been

151
00:08:38,510 --> 00:08:40,549
pondering over this all afternoon.

152
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,840
I think you've got a point.

153
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:45,750
What do you mean?

154
00:08:47,510 --> 00:08:48,840
Back then, you asked me

155
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:51,790
if I ever thought about

156
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:54,600
treating Mi Si's

157
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,840
stealing problem.

158
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,200
You have no idea.

159
00:09:04,030 --> 00:09:05,870
I don't know what else I can do.

160
00:09:06,510 --> 00:09:07,320
Hello.

161
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,390
It's impossible to stop her in time.

162
00:09:30,390 --> 00:09:32,000
I'm really afraid

163
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,400
she'll end up in jail again
because of this.

164
00:09:36,630 --> 00:09:37,960
If we could

165
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,480
root out

166
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,870
this problem,

167
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:44,080
that would be great.

168
00:09:44,270 --> 00:09:45,000
Yeah,

169
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,660
it would definitely be good
if it could be cured.

170
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:54,150
Can her problem really be cured?

171
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:55,510
Sure.

172
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,550
There are actually many patients

173
00:09:58,550 --> 00:09:59,750
with this condition.

174
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:01,120
And I've seen

175
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,240
many real-life cases in a book.

176
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,840
Honestly,

177
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:06,910
her problem is much easier to cure

178
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:08,750
than mine and Ai Chen's.

179
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:14,840
Could you teach me how to cure it?

180
00:10:18,270 --> 00:10:19,080
San.

181
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,790
What are you doing?

182
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,010
I'm looking for something.

183
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,790
There was one time

184
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,150
when you were grabbing things

185
00:10:32,150 --> 00:10:33,200
in the supermarket

186
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,750
and got caught on camera.

187
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,500
I paid them money to settle it,

188
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,510
got the video back,

189
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:40,600
and made a disc of it.

190
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,530
But I can't remember where I put it.

191
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,030
Did that happen?

192
00:10:44,870 --> 00:10:46,070
Why don't I remember?

193
00:10:47,390 --> 00:10:49,200
You just don't want to remember.

194
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,480
Why are you looking for it?

195
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:52,320
I...

196
00:10:52,870 --> 00:10:53,670
I'm just...

197
00:10:54,390 --> 00:10:56,270
I'm just trying to cure your problem.

198
00:10:56,270 --> 00:10:57,750
What's your problem?

199
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,200
You've been influenced by those two.

200
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:02,030
Well, look,

201
00:11:02,750 --> 00:11:03,720
Liu Zhengliang

202
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:04,630
actually has some skills.

203
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:06,870
I hate whoever says I have a problem.

204
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,570
Okay, let's not say you have a problem.

205
00:11:09,870 --> 00:11:10,670
Let's just say

206
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,600
we'll find a way

207
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:14,750
to correct your little bad habit.

208
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:15,810
I won't correct it.

209
00:11:16,670 --> 00:11:18,270
I'm already this old.

210
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:21,790
Well, aren't you curious?

211
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,910
Don't you want to know what exactly

212
00:11:23,910 --> 00:11:25,110
Liu Zhengliang said?

213
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,030
Let's hear it.

214
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:36,640
[1314 Funeral Services]

215
00:11:33,550 --> 00:11:34,280
Just this...

216
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,520
What do you want to do?

217
00:11:37,870 --> 00:11:39,600
Well, um,

218
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,120
I'll find that disc,

219
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:43,080
and then you watch the video. Um...

220
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,440
As soon as you see yourself

221
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,550
grabbing something,

222
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:46,880
you just slap yourself.

223
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,150
You see it, and you

224
00:11:48,150 --> 00:11:49,120
slap yourself.

225
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:53,870
Um, this is called aversion therapy.

226
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:55,550
Basically,

227
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:57,270
once you slap yourself,

228
00:11:57,270 --> 00:11:58,790
this stimulation

229
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,120
will...

230
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,360
will suppress your satisfaction

231
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:04,480
of grabbing things.

232
00:12:06,150 --> 00:12:07,440
You want to electrocute me?

233
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:08,110
No, no...

234
00:12:08,150 --> 00:12:10,120
No, you can't
electrocute anyone with this.

235
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:10,870
It just...

236
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:12,550
hurts a little.

237
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:19,420
[To the second floor]

238
00:12:18,670 --> 00:12:19,510
Stop there!

239
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:23,790
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

240
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:24,670
It doesn't hurt?
If it doesn't hurt, why are you running?

241
00:12:24,670 --> 00:12:25,730
What's wrong, Mom?

242
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:28,080
Go get your dad's clothes.

243
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,720
Amy!

244
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:42,550
"I, Yang Guo, swear that my heart

245
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:46,320
only belongs to you,
now and forever, Auntie.

246
00:12:46,630 --> 00:12:48,150
If I ever betray you,

247
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:50,120
you don't even need to kill me.

248
00:12:50,630 --> 00:12:52,750
I will kill myself immediately."

249
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,000
After saying that,

250
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,320
he broke out in a cold sweat

251
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,790
and just gave himself

252
00:12:58,790 --> 00:13:00,390
2 heavy slaps.

253
00:13:03,150 --> 00:13:04,550
Do you believe in vows?

254
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:06,320
Nope.

255
00:13:06,510 --> 00:13:07,840
If vows meant anything,

256
00:13:07,910 --> 00:13:10,270
the old factory director
at my mom's workplace

257
00:13:10,270 --> 00:13:12,400
would have gotten his karma years ago.

258
00:13:17,150 --> 00:13:17,910
Jia Xin.

259
00:13:21,870 --> 00:13:23,200
I can't see anything.

260
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:25,200
I can only listen.

261
00:13:27,150 --> 00:13:27,960
No matter

262
00:13:28,790 --> 00:13:30,320
what happens in the future,

263
00:13:30,630 --> 00:13:31,870
don't ever lie to me.

264
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,320
Okay.

265
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:43,360
Alright.

266
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:45,630
That's it for today?

267
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:47,960
It's about time

268
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,240
for me to go to work.

269
00:13:51,550 --> 00:13:52,270
Can you take me

270
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:53,800
to your workplace with you?

271
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:54,790
Nope.

272
00:13:55,030 --> 00:13:55,840
No, no.

273
00:13:56,150 --> 00:13:58,200
My workplace is ominous.

274
00:13:58,910 --> 00:14:00,370
I don't buy superstition.

275
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:01,550
Now that you've

276
00:14:01,550 --> 00:14:02,810
gotten to know my work,

277
00:14:02,870 --> 00:14:04,270
I also want to visit

278
00:14:04,270 --> 00:14:05,240
your workplace.

279
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:11,650
[Moxibustion Care] [A healthy physique
starts with good self-care]

280
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,700
I have to work all night

281
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,480
and can't leave halfway.

282
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:11,970
How will you get back then?

283
00:14:12,390 --> 00:14:13,920
I have the day off tomorrow.

284
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,870
We can chat all night long.

285
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:20,140
[Moxibustion Care] [A healthy physique
starts with good self-care]

286
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:20,200
But...

287
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,720
Why so many buts?

288
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,320
If you don't want to, just say it.

289
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,390
I want to. I really want to.

290
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:29,880
[West Gate]

291
00:14:33,290 --> 00:14:40,740
[Security Department]

292
00:14:35,670 --> 00:14:36,630
Here we are.

293
